+# The only file an escalation report is allowed to change.
+#
+# THIS IS THE LOAD-BEARING HALF OF THE SAFETY CHECK, so it is worth saying why.
+# A report reports: AGENTS-CHARTER.md S3 puts findings in AGENT-LOG.md, and
+# PR #19 said so in its own body -- "Log entry only. No code is changed by this
+# pull request." A pull request that changes anything else is a CHANGE, and a
+# change is something somebody intends to merge. Emitting `Closes #N` against
+# one of those silently closes it the moment the fix lands, and closing syntax
+# is not something the merge gate can see or refuse.
+ESCALATION_REPORT_FILES = frozenset(["AGENT-LOG.md"])
 
+# AGENTS-CHARTER.md S3: "ESCALATE entries carry ESCALATED". Matched
+# case-sensitively as a whole word so that PROSE about escalation does not read
+# as a declaration of one -- PR #26's own title, "close the escalation report
+# automatically when its fix merges", must not match, and does not.
+_ESCALATION_MARKER = re.compile(r"\bESCALATED?\b")
 
